want to do a couple interesting polling  stories not just normal polling stories  about the horse race but polling stories  that really go to a lot of what is  underlying sentiment in the United  States right now in our political system  yesterday I mentioned to you that 49% of  Americans in a recent poll said that  impeachment proceedings should start  against Donald Trump this by itself is  already a stunning number but it's sort  of softened I guess you could say by the  reality that starting impeachment  proceedings isn't necessarily saying  Trump should be removed  you might just believe there's enough  evidence to warrant starting those  proceedings but you're sort of open to  whatever conclusion those proceedings  might come to that was yesterday there  is now a new poll which says that 47% of  Americans straight-up  think that Donald Trump should be  removed from office period and with  every one of these polls that are  historically shocking like this is  historically a shocking number my shock  continues to be that only 47% of  Americans believe that Donald Trump  should be removed from office which gets  me back to what I said yesterday which  actually I would you know most of the  time when I say something negative about  a group of voters even if it's a group  of voters that most people in our  audience disagree with I will get some  emails from people saying you know David  you really it's better if you don't say  that the optics aren't good about you  saying I did not get that when I said  yesterday if you don't believe that this  man is a systemic danger to the United  States and to the world that you were  part of the problem and that's where I  returned today if you think that what's  going on right now is even remotely okay  you are either unaware of what's going  on  sort of like an ignorance is bliss type  of thing or you are part of the problem  because it's embarrassing that merely  47% of the country thinks that Donald  Trump should be removed from office  40% 47% is a high number looking back at  other presidents  but it is way way way too low  considering what it is that we're  dealing with today and I was interested  in looking at this in the context of  history as a point of historical  comparison I went back to Richard Nixon  because increasingly we see more and  more sort of parallels between Watergate  and the Trump Fiasco administration  presidency  I believe that when Richard Nixon  ultimately resigned somewhere between 55  and 57 percent of the country believed  that he should be removed so the numbers  are not that far from that point so most  importantly step one here no matter  where you are on impeachment indictment  resignation removal under the 25th  amendment the agenda of Trump and his  cronies you need to vote every single  one of them out in November every single  one that is up for re-election needs to  be voted out in November that's just a  little over seven weeks to go then we  need to have this conversation about  what is wrong with the people of this  country because something is very wrong  that only 47 percent think that it's  time for Trump to go and we've talked  about there's all sorts of these rules  of thumb and politics like 20% of the  population will always support the  president 20% will never support the  president it's the other 60% that can  sort of be swayed by what actually  happens and that's probably a factor in  in what these numbers are  I think that these circumstances are so  extenuating and so outrageous that they  really should be going well above and  beyond what these historical numbers  have been and when it comes when it  comes to Watergate by the way I think  that the the Watergate comparison is apt  not in terms of the seriousness or scope  of what was done we at this point know  what it was that Richard Nixon did we  don't yet know what it is that Donald  Trump and his cronies have done  the parable the parallel nature of  Watergate and Trump includes the way in  which Trump's behavior has become  increasingly erratic as a result of the  investigation the ways in which Donald  Trump has tried to suppress that  investigation in the way that we saw  done during Richard Nixon's time the  ways in which Donald Trump has turned  the investigators themselves into the  enemy even though there's not any  evidence that they're actually the ones  guilty of wrongdoing so there are  definitely parallels in terms of the  subject matter in terms of what was done  by who and when we're gonna have to wait  and see but what I do want to talk about  next and this is the next poll we're  going to discuss today relates exactly  to the smearing of the investigators  this episode is sponsored in part by  better help calm slash Pakman which  gives you access to a fully licensed and  experienced psychologist or therapist  through video phone and text I know from  the emails I get that in our audience  like in the broader world there are  people who are struggling with different  issues in their lives and many of them  choose not to talk to somebody about it  either for financial reasons for reasons  of stigma associated with seeking out a  therapist and I think it's really  important to do everything you can to  get past that because it's really  important to talk to someone when you  feel like that's the right thing to do  and what better help calm provides is  number one the elimination of the stigma  that could be associated with it you  work through video phone whichever  method is best for you you also will be  able to save money compared to seeing an  in-person therapist and it is so easy to  get started that I encourage you to go  to better help calm slash Pakman a few  questions that you answer which will get  you paired up with a therapist that  meets your needs you can always switch  to somebody else if you don't feel as  though the match is a good fit and it is  something that everyone  should have access to go to better help  calm slash Pakman it's easy to sign up  it's easy to get started we've put a  link in the description if you're  watching on YouTube and once again that  website is better help calm /pa que ma n

